Ben & Jerry's Marshmallow Sky ice cream is a scoop shop only flavour available in the US. It's hidden behind a magic door where no one can go and see how it's made but........ we've created it here for you so you can finally see what it's like and how to make it. 
#loveourtubs #icecream

What is it?
It's a vanilla ice cream coloured with blue spirulina, chocolate chip cookie dough, double chocolate chip cookie dough AND marshmallow swirls. Not only does it look amazing but it tastes amazing too. 

What you'll need to make it....
Ice Cream:
400ml Milk (2% fat)
300ml Cream (49% fat)
65g Sugar
65g Dextrose
1/2tsp spirulina mixed with 1tsp water (added when cold)
3x 25g Marshmallows which have GELATIN (important!)
2-3 tsp Vanilla extract
25g Skimmed Milk Powder

Chocolate Chip Cookie Dough:
60g Unsalted butter at room temperature
45g Sugar
40g Brown sugar
1/2 tsp Salt
2 tbsp Heavy cream (whatever you have)
2 tbsp Golden Syrup (corn syrup)
1 tsp vanilla extract
70g Plain flour baked at 350°F (180°C) for 10 minutes (all purpose flour)
45g semi-sweet chocolate, chopped into bits

Double Chocolate Chip Cookie Dough:
60g Unsalted butter at room temperature
45g Sugar
40g Brown sugar
1/2 tsp Salt
2 tbsp Heavy cream (whatever you have)
2 tbsp Golden Syrup
1 tsp vanilla extract
50g Plain flour baked at 350°F (180°C) for 10 minutes (all purpose flour)
20g Cocoa Powder
45g semi-sweet chocolate, chopped into bits

Marshmallow Swirl:
Egg white x 2
1/4 tsp Cream of Tatar 
100g Sugar

Now if that isn't a HUGE list of ingredients, I don't know what is. Don't let it worry you though, it's all pretty easy to do. 😊

These are Salt & Straw cookie dough's though 😉 just don't tell B&J's!

The video will show you how to make it and if you do, we'd love to hear about it. 

